Z||000000||fierovette||07-19-2001||08:26 AM||||Any ideas on what to use, or what type of plug to put in the holes when removing the rear wing? Black GT, some type of plug for temporary use, that also looks good.This way, on occasion, I can run without the wing. For a different look, and keep water out.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Galen||07-19-2001||09:04 AM||||some ducttape? or if you wanna go namebrand. 'Duck' Tape<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"It may be the opinion of the court, but its still wrong"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.22 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||07-19-2001||09:57 AM||||I would go to Radio Shack (or another type of electronics supply store) and find some black plastic panel plugs that are sized to fit the holes. (The type of round plugs used to fill the hole when a toggle switch or round push button are removed from a panel.)<P>They're usually black textured plastic and *very* slightly domed (almost flat), and they would look very professional. You could even prime and paint them to match the color of the car, and they would probably look like a factory-provided item to someone who didn't know otherwise.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||07-19-2001||10:09 AM||||Yeah, kinda like the plugs used to cover the antenna holes on police cruisers.  They actually don't look too bad.  I'd paint them though.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||07-19-2001||10:30 AM||||You guys must've been reading my mind (good for a short read)!  I've been wondering about how to cover the spoiler holes, and make it look "clean."  Would be great to be able to switch back and forth, from "spoiler" to "clean" decklid, especially on my GT.    <BR> <BR>Thanks for the great idea  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!||||reg||10
