Z||000006||fierovette||07-20-2001||07:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>I would go to Radio Shack (or another type of electronics supply store) and find some black plastic panel plugs that are sized to fit the holes. (The type of round plugs used to fill the hole when a toggle switch or round push button are removed from a panel.)<P>They're usually black textured plastic and *very* slightly domed (almost flat), and they would look very professional. You could even prime and paint them to match the color of the car, and they would probably look like a factory-provided item to someone who didn't know otherwise.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Excellent, Just the ticket, guess it works for others too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cozmo||07-20-2001||08:09 AM||||Try the plastic license plate nuts and bolts sold at auto parts stores and Wally World.  They're cheap, come in a lot of colors and can be easily water sealed with a spot of silicone RTV.  <BR>PLUS....<BR>If ya wanna go fer the "custom" look, they come in chrome and gold...even neon!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>{b]C02M0[/b]||||reg||1
